      "content": "The state mismatch is now only a warning that the user can dismiss by choosing \"Store\". Combined with the nonce no longer being reset/rotated, this effectively removes the state validation guarantee. An attacker who can trigger the auth callback URI with an arbitrary token and a mismatched state can get the user to store an attacker-controlled token. At minimum, keep the hard failure for mismatched state, or clearly scope the bypass to the intended external-signin flow (e.g. only when no auth request is in progress)."
